00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
How long I stood there for, I do not know. 

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
This was so different from everything I had imagined. 

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:26.000
I remembered other travellers telling tales about London. Bright colourful tales of a grand wealthy city full of possibilities, full of travellers like me. 

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
They had made it sound so exciting, so dreamy, so welcoming. 

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Not this cold, loud, busy place where I clearly didn’t belong. 

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:48.000
I looked at the birds around me. The crows, the blackbirds, the pigeons, the magpies… they were at home here, in a world of black and white. 

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
My green feathers made me feel so alien, I could feel everyone looking at me. 

00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:01.000
The shame made my heart race: I felt so scruffy after the flight, if only I could find a place to wash? 

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:08.000
But that big wide river looked so wild, so grey, it was as terrifying as the rest. 

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
For a moment, I thought of turning back. 

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:18.000
I toyed with that idea. Wouldn’t it be nice to see the sun again, to see my mom, my friends? 

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.000
But I didn’t have the strength. Not yet. 

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:32.000
And what would I tell them? I would have to make up a story, a good story, maybe that’s what the other travellers did too. 

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:44.000
The grey pavement lay bare in front of me. Not a blade of grass. Not a leaf. Not a sign of life. Only waste left by the humans. 

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:54.000
I picked up a plastic straw. It felt strange in my beak. Strange, but strangely familiar. 

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.000
I examined it closely. 

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
With a bit of imagination, it could look like a twig. 

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:09.000
With a bit of imagination, maybe one could use it to build a nest. 

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Not the kind of nest I had imagined, of course, probably a bit smaller. 

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.000
But with a bit of imagination, and with time, maybe one day that nest could look like home.
